mall Blind, you act first pre-flop but will act last on all subsequent rounds (the Button), giving you a significant positional advantage. Playing passively by just calling often allows the opponent to see a flop for free or control the pace. Given your hand strength and positional advantage, taking the initiative is the optimal strategy. Raising puts pressure on the opponent and builds the pot when you likely have the best hand.\n\nReason: QTo is strong enough to play for value. A minimum raise to 200 chips leverages your position, denies the opponent a "cheap" look at the flop with weak hands, and establishes aggression which is crucial since you are currently trailing in the cumulative chip count.\n\nAnswer: 200'}
